comments[6]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-05T06:44:04.265Z",codex-sol,"All eight findings verified as valid. Plan: pin actions and disable checkout credentials; default-off owner release gate; read-only preparation/checks/pack with artifact handoff to privileged publication; same-day refusal; trusted HTTPS credential destinations; expected malformed-URL error; option validation before inference; folded-scalar interpolation regression tests. Publishing retains only contents and pull-requests writes for protected release metadata plus OIDC; no actions write, dependency installs or repository scripts."
  "2026-10-05T06:52:17.790Z",codex-sol,"Initial full release:check passed: 98 tests, zero failures/skips, all nine authored source files at 100% statements/branches/functions/lines; lint, duplication (0%), docstrings, typecheck, production audit, pack dry-run, changelog and publish-attestation passed. Actionlint 1.7.12 passed CI/release/CodeQL workflows. Runtime findings 4181327596/4181327600/4181327602 fixed with regression coverage; workflow findings 4181327570/4181327572/4181327583/4181327585/4181327609 fixed. Existing protected metadata PR flow is retained; actions-write automation removed; Bun acceptance is a separate read-only job. OIDC preflight precedes remote writes; local version preparation occurs without write credentials."
  "2026-10-05T06:54:02.287Z",codex-sol,"Artifact handoff shell was exercised with a synthetic metadata bundle: valid commit/tree/hash passed; changed tarball bytes, commit, tree and base all failed before loading release metadata. Same-day shell regression covers first release, unchanged skip, and changed duplicate standard/suffixed tags. Existing registry recovery verifies only attestation presence; exact artifact/subject verification is outside these findings and tracked in pm-jev-5jw9."
  "2026-10-05T06:54:46.585Z",codex-sol,"Linked npm run test:install passed: packed npm/Node and Bun library imports, npx/bunx installed-extension live triage, compact/full CLI output, negative JSON gate and secret/clean safety gate exit codes. Fixtures used local tev1 and synthetic data; no hosted acceptance or npm publication. Strict pm health --strict-exit --require-merge-drivers --json passed with zero warnings/findings. PM linked-test result tracking is disabled, so durable results are recorded in comments and the review receipt."
  "2026-10-05T06:56:47.031Z",codex-sol,The final linked release gate caught one duplicate shell-extraction snippet introduced by the added handoff regression. Refactored it into one test helper without changing the 0% gate. The duplication gate now passes; rerunning the full linked release gate on the corrected suite.
  "2026-10-05T06:58:25.097Z",codex-sol,"Final linked npm run release:check passed with 99 tests and zero failures/skips; 100/100/100/100 across all nine authored sources, lint, zero duplication, docstrings, typecheck, production audit, pack contents, changelog and attestation all passed. Publishing retains actions: read only to diagnose pending release PR runs, never actions: write; focused workflow suite (15/15) and Actionlint passed after this minimal read permission correction. All eight comment IDs are fixed, with dispositions in docs/pr-1-review-findings.md. Items remain in_progress/open for orchestrator verification. Open boundaries: actual OIDC/protected-PR execution untested; registry recovery identity verification deferred in pm-jev-5jw9."
